{"severity":"error","file":"errors/deterministic_violation_3.march","start_line":12,"start_col":4,"end_line":12,"end_col":18,"message":"`mod Sim` (declared `cap deterministic`) declares `needs IO.Clock`, which admits the clock, a nondeterminism source, directly or through a stdlib wrapper such as `DateTime.now`.\n\nDeclare only capabilities that are neither the clock nor an RNG (`IO.Console`, `IO.FileRead`, ...), and move the code that reads the clock or an RNG to a module without `cap deterministic`.","code":"deterministic_violation","fix":null,"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"CONTRACT"}
